WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.730
A security control is a safeguard or countermeasure designed to reduce risk.

2
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:10.058
Controls can be technical, operational, managerial, or privacy-focused.

3
00:00:10.058 --> 00:00:18.020
Technical controls may include access control mechanisms, logging, encryption, network protections, and system hardening.

4
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:24.426
Operational controls may include incident response procedures, training programs, and account reviews.

5
00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:30.722
Managerial controls support governance, planning, risk assessment, authorization, and oversight.

6
00:00:30.722 --> 00:00:39.282
Together, these controls help organizations protect systems, detect problems, respond to incidents, and recover from disruptions.

7
00:00:39.282 --> 00:00:41.288
A control is more than a label.

8
00:00:41.288 --> 00:00:47.265
It needs ownership, implementation, evidence, assessment, and maintenance to be useful in practice.
